=== test_proof.py ===
[derived] the ledger stores observations only — there is no level field for anyone to set by hand
[ladder] a level requires every level beneath it: live evidence alone stayed at IMPLEMENTED until the acceptance tests passed
[regression] editing the code dropped OFFLINE VERIFIED -> IMPLEMENTED automatically, and restoring it brought the level back — nobody touched a status
[failure] a failing run is recorded as failing — the ledger keeps both, so a regression is visible rather than overwritten
[expiry] live and stress evidence older than its window expired automatically and the badge fell back to OFFLINE VERIFIED — a green light cannot rot into a lie by sitting still
[stability] the code hash survives line-ending translation while still changing on real edits
[registry] 20 declared capabilities each state a user capability, invariants, code and tests; nothing with unwritten code claims a level above SPEC
PASS test_proof

=== test_mission.py ===
[persisted] the mission contract is a file on disk, not a passage in a transcript that compaction can summarise away
[compaction+restart] the window was wiped and a brand-new process recompiled the identical objective, criteria and binding constraints from disk
[model-swap] the contract names no model or provider, so swapping one cannot change what the mission is
[bound] an action must name the criterion it serves and the evidence it will produce; unbound work and unrecognisable outcomes are both refused
[monotonic] met evidence cannot silently vanish: invalidating it needed a stated reason and the original record is still there
[amendment] the objective cannot be edited in place — the change carries a reason, an author, and both fingerprints, so drift is visible instead of silent
[gaps] 4 blocker dimensions classified and routed; only the authority gap escalated to the owner
[every-role] practitioner, student and consultant all receive the objective, the binding constraints and their criterion — the memory router cannot route the assignment away
[closure] a mission closes on met criteria, never on a decision to stop; and a mission with no criteria cannot be created
[unblock] a raised blocker can be resolved through the CLI with the reason recorded, and a bad index fails loudly — resolve_blocker was written but unreachable from every surface
PASS test_mission

