[artifacts] the scorer reads what the task actually wrote from its own step record, not from a guess
[gate] two identical artifacts, one gate failure: the failure cannot win at any score
[interface] the considered page scored 1.0 and the generated filler 0.2963, both passing the same gate
[applies] a citation to a nonexistent atom sank its candidate; the same check stayed silent about an interface
[isolation] an attempt's changes were undone byte-for-byte, including deleting the file it invented
[promote] the winning attempt's bytes were put back and every attempt kept its own score on disk
[adaptive] one attempt until something fails, then 3, then 5 — capped by the owner's setting and switchable off
[explain] the winner is reported with the reason every loser lost
[wired] the loop stashes every refused attempt (15 of them here) and promotes one only when it strictly beats the last — on a task where the verifier cannot discriminate it reports a tie and changes nothing, which is the honest answer rather than a shuffle
[discriminates] a real answer scores 1.0, a one-character one 0.75, an unfinished one carrying TODO 0.75, and a .json that does not parse 0.6 — the composite can now tell attempts apart on ordinary work, where every other component declines to answer and six attempts previously tied at 0.0
[contained] a planted stash could not overwrite prompts/constitution.md nor write outside the expert root, a traversal artifact was refused and RECORDED, and the score that decides which attempt wins is control state while the attempt's own files stay the agent's
